{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987108-stats-for-consilium-npcs","id":987108,"title":"Stats for Consilium NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T22:38:14-07:00","id":987108,"title":"Stats for Consilium NPCs","content":"Having wrapped up our first campaign and now starting our second, I've decided to introduce Consilium representatives to the Chronicle. To those who have designed Consilium NPCs, how much XP give or take do you assign for Sentinels, Provosts, and Councilors respectively? Which stats and merits do you prioritize? Would you agree that 5-dot Arcana are solely the purview of Councilors?<br /> <br /> Clearly they've seen and accomplished much more in their Awakened 'career'. Would love your insights!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T00:01:59-07:00","id":987121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987108-stats-for-consilium-npcs#post987108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which stats and merits do you prioritize?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just stick to Gnosis, Arcana, legacy and any unique merits that'll have an immediate impact on the character. I mean, most of the Consilium are generally going to be non-combatants so their stats aren't that important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you agree that 5-dot Arcana are solely the purview of Councilors? </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Boston Unveiled goes that root, but there's a tendency in the Order books for the really high-ranking members to not actually hold any office because it uses up time that could be spent doing master stuff. The offices get filled with Adepts who are the apprentices of masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:47:30-07:00","id":987192,"title":"","content":"I'm copy-pasting this from the place I wrote it, because it's relevant here too (but adding a section to the end to actually answer your question).<br /> <br /> Probably not exactly what you're looking for, but in the past, whenever I've used such a thing, I've always ended up having to make the character more real because I ended up involving them much, much more than I had initially thought I would. I like to make everything in my games connect to itself and to a central theme, so when I've eventually needed a character who's the niece of the X or who will take over the business from Y, it's been the previously generic character that the PCs spoke to for five minutes and for some reason really liked. So I've stopped using those sorts of generic characters and I just make them complex real people from the beginning, since I have to end up making them complex with backstories eventually anyway. Just a thought, I know it's not what you were looking for. But my thought is that if incorporating politicians in your chronicle is important enough that you're thinking about stats, why not make them real human beings and incorporate them more?<br /> <br /> Still, I know this isn't what you asked for, so I'm posting the link to the hyper-political DC game I ran the first time I ever ran a game. Feel free to use my Consilium rules or the Councilors:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://the-freshman-class.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://the-freshman-class.obsidianportal.com/</a><br /> <br /> Their character sheets are under &quot;characters&quot;, but there's also a narrative breakdown under the Wiki. Go to &quot;Consilium of Washington, DC&quot; and then &quot;Consilium Leadership&quot; if you'd like to see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 10-14-2016, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:46:46-07:00","id":987274,"title":"","content":"terpsichordean&gt; For the sake of simplicity, I typically do their Power, Finesse, and Resistance traits the same way you would do when creating a spirit or ghost. I jot down a few dice pools for their used skills, and of course everything pertaining to the Mage Template that you'd see come into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:47:54-07:00","id":987314,"title":"","content":"I create the stats of NPCs as-needed; generally spinning off &quot;What are their great/average/worst dice pools?&quot; and rolling with that.<br /> <br /> Most Consilia only have one or two masters, with the Caucuses tending to have slightly more (usually three to five) if they cover a wide area or less if they don't. If the Caucus does have a master, though, they're usually fairly potent. That's my general ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}